- [President Jokowi Orders Kanjuruhan Fact-finding Team to Reveal Investigation Results in One Month](https://setkab.go.id/en/president-jokowi-orders-kanjuruhan-fact-finding-team-to-reveal-investigation-results-in-one-month/) - Jokowi ordered the independent fact-finding team to disclose its findings within one month and the government issued a presidential decree to support the investigation.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"President Jokowi Orders Kanjuruhan Fact-finding Team to Reveal Investigation Results in One Month","publisher":"Sekretariat Kabinet Republik Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-10-04","url":"https://setkab.go.id/en/president-jokowi-orders-kanjuruhan-fact-finding-team-to-reveal-investigation-results-in-one-month/","claim":"Jokowi ordered the independent fact-finding team to disclose its findings within one month and the government issued a presidential decree to support the investigation.","locator":"lines 37-40","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct official transcript of Jokowi's directive and the government's response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Immediate follow-up to the Kanjuruhan disaster in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct Jokowi directive via the Cabinet Secretariat report.","contrary_evidence":["A fast investigation does not guarantee independent or complete accountability.","The article does not show the eventual legal outcome."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.9"]}

- [Kanjuruhan Fact-Finding Team Reports Results of Investigation to President Jokowi](https://setkab.go.id/en/kanjuruhan-fact-finding-team-reports-results-of-investigation-to-president-jokowi/) - the fact-finding team handed Jokowi a 124-page report that identified legal and moral responsibility and recommended that police continue criminal investigations of suspected persons responsible for the tragedy.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Kanjuruhan Fact-Finding Team Reports Results of Investigation to President Jokowi","publisher":"Sekretariat Kabinet Republik Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-10-14","url":"https://setkab.go.id/en/kanjuruhan-fact-finding-team-reports-results-of-investigation-to-president-jokowi/","claim":"The fact-finding team handed Jokowi a 124-page report that identified legal and moral responsibility and recommended that police continue criminal investigations of suspected persons responsible for the tragedy.","locator":"lines 37-46","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct official record of the team briefing the president and summarizing the report's conclusions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 follow-up to the Kanjuruhan disaster.","ruler_attribution":"Direct report to Jokowi and presidential oversight of the response.","contrary_evidence":["Recommendation and reporting are not the same as completed justice.","The article does not indicate whether recommendations were fully implemented."],"lenses":["3B.4","3B.9","3B.10"]}

- [Police use of tear gas triggered Kanjuruhan stampede: Komnas HAM](https://en.antaranews.com/news/258265/police-use-of-tear-gas-triggered-kanjuruhan-stampede-komnas-ham) - Komnas HAM concluded that police tear gas was the main trigger for the Kanjuruhan stampede, said the police fired tear gas 45 times, and noted the disaster killed 135 people including children.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Police use of tear gas triggered Kanjuruhan stampede: Komnas HAM","publisher":"ANTARA News","publication_date":"2022-11-02","url":"https://en.antaranews.com/news/258265/police-use-of-tear-gas-triggered-kanjuruhan-stampede-komnas-ham","claim":"Komnas HAM concluded that police tear gas was the main trigger for the Kanjuruhan stampede, said the police fired tear gas 45 times, and noted the disaster killed 135 people including children.","locator":"lines 63-81","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous report of Komnas HAM's public findings with specific casualty and force details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 fact finding about a major domestic protection failure.","ruler_attribution":"The abuse was committed by security forces under Jokowi's national administration, not by Jokowi personally.","contrary_evidence":["The article reports institutional findings rather than a direct presidential order.","It captures a single disaster, not the whole year."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.9","3B.10"]}

- [Indonesia: End harassment of residents opposed to 'national strategic project'](https://www.amnesty.id/kabar-terbaru/siaran-pers/indonesia-end-harassment-of-residents-opposed-to-national-strategic-project/02/2022/) - Amnesty said the Wadas quarry operation was tied to a dam Jokowi had designated a national strategic project, and that hundreds of security personnel entering the village caused fear, with videos showing arbitrary detentions and beatings of residents.
  SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Indonesia: End harassment of residents opposed to 'national strategic project'","publisher":"Amnesty International Indonesia","publication_date":"2022-02-10","url":"https://www.amnesty.id/kabar-terbaru/siaran-pers/indonesia-end-harassment-of-residents-opposed-to-national-strategic-project/02/2022/","claim":"Amnesty said the Wadas quarry operation was tied to a dam Jokowi had designated a national strategic project, and that hundreds of security personnel entering the village caused fear, with videos showing arbitrary detentions and beatings of residents.","locator":"lines 45-53","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed contemporaneous human-rights reporting with resident video corroboration and explicit ruler attribution for the project.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 domestic protest and land-rights confrontation.","ruler_attribution":"Jokowi's project designation and the security deployment make the issue ruler-relevant, though local police/tactical units carried out the abuse.","contrary_evidence":["The article is advocacy-oriented and does not establish a direct presidential order to use force.","The project itself is not evidence of violence absent the security response."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.5","3B.7","3B.8","3B.9"]}

- [Amnesty International Report 2022/23; The State of the World's Human Rights; Indonesia 2022](https://www.amnesty.org/en/location/asia-and-the-pacific/south-east-asia-and-the-pacific/indonesia/report-indonesia/) - Amnesty reported that on 12 February 2022 police shot dead 21-year-old Erfaldi during a protest against a gold-mining operation, using tear gas and live ammunition to disperse hundreds of people; a police-officer trial was still ongoing at year's end.
